title Caravan refer -- a long-standing quarrel goes before a hand that is neither party
prompt Keaton set the loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the operator card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota doc, condense REMEMBER when a set closes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md whole -- every living row closed: %96 and %97 released last lap, %81, %83, %84, %85 each carrying a closure note that names its proof. No open agent-closable red stands, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think Read the running thread from the top three rows of the log index. The newest recommend named the open question exactly: the arc now publishes a long-standing quarrel where the outcome is read, and nothing in it asks the plan to do anything differently about that -- a supervisor may announce an old objection forever and still run exactly as it always ran.
think Weighed what a plan can honestly owe a quarrel without breaking the arc's own discipline. A plan answering its own quarrel is the supervisor grading an objection raised against itself, which every rung of this arc refuses. A plan staying its whole record under an objection would break the standing generalization test the arc measures by. What a plan can honestly do is change who has seen the argument -- carry the case, once, to a hand that has not spoken.
think Named it refer, under the Comlink tendency -- a plain English verb meaning exactly to put a matter before somebody else to weigh. Grepped the tree: no collision with any seated module, waymark, or Caravan rung.
think Designed the forum as a byte a run only ever reads. The whole load-bearing idea is that a supervisor may not name the hand that weighs an objection against it, so plan.forum is seated by an operator before any quarrel exists, and ReferUnaddressed refuses by name where nothing stands there -- a configuration reachable by argument alone, which is what makes that guard real rather than decorative.
think Gave the rung a fifth refusal rather than the four its neighbors carry, since ReferParty is the rung itself: a case landing in the box of the reader who raised the quarrel wears the look of a hearing while being none. Four would have folded the point into a general miscount.
think Chose to copy the case rather than summarize it -- the plan's word, the standing, the age, all three off the wire in the run that sends them -- because a summary is exactly where a supervisor would get to shade the argument against itself.
think Ordered the referring last of all, after the heralding whose standing it carries out, and after a relenting that may already have taken down the quarrel a case would be built from.
think Built the rung the arc's way: refer.rye seeded from swell.rye, the swelling section converted to re-exports, a new Report layer wrapping swell's, and the referring section written fresh. Six RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim.
obs The measurement moves and nothing else does. One plan of 6 phases run twice absorbs 3, loses 3, re-seats 3, spends 6 dependents, takes the same judgment back, posts and carries the same correction, reads the same reply, records the same disagreement, escorts the same word, asks the same reader, stands the same mark, tells the same raiser, carries the same position past itself, dates it to the same age of 4, publishes the same loud standing, and settles carried either way -- while long-standing quarrels carried to a hand that is neither party rise 0 to 1 and long-standing quarrels nobody outside the argument ever sees fall 1 to 0.
obs A case, once carried, belongs to the desk it landed on. It survives a provisioning, as every record of a quarrel does, and it survives the withdrawal of the quarrel itself, which nothing else in this arc does. A supervisor able to take a case back off a third hand's desk would have shown somebody a document and then closed their hand around it. Proven as its own fold, outside any run.
obs The planted control is the honest part of the round. Disarm every guard at once -- the write skipped, the read-back skipped, and both harness reads of the desk -- and the selftest prints GREEN while caravan/.readers/bench.case does not exist at all, beside a quarrel four runs old still reading loud on plan.standing. An operator would believe a third hand had the case in front of them. Seeing that once is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
obs The lap turned its own ratchet twice. Adding one parameter pushed run_in_refer to 72 lines, past the tree-wide seventy; gathering the six quarrel words into one Quarrel shape brought it back under, which reads better than the list it replaced. The harness then split at its own seam into seat_the_wire and seat_the_history. The past-70 roster is clean.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 20, context/QUIN.md, taken as choir count 74 mod 27. Since last lap read it beside item 19, ORGANIZING.md was deep-read as the genuine second reading. Its filing law is what put the cairn before the REMEMBER condensation rather than after it, and what kept the departing swell prose one git show away rather than merely deleted.
loom witness=caravan_refer_witness rungs_sung=74 refer_module_lines=9346 red_paths_on_metal=6 measurement_before=1 measurement_after=0
file caravan/refer.rye the rung -- the forum read off the wire, the party refused by name, the case copied rather than summarized, the referring last of all
file tools/caravan_refer_witness.rish the witness -- the two-plan lap, the case read from the forum's own box outside the run that wrote it, the reader's box proven empty
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir grows to 74, roster bijection whole
file caravan/README.md the durable per-rung account of what refer proves and why each guard exists
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge refilled, the swell edge condensed to a pointer, git nib pinned in the work commit
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back at 7f69316945, recorded before the card was swept
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, says how long a standing one has stood, reads that age aloud where an operator opens the outcome, and finally puts a long-standing one before a hand that is neither party -- so the question above is what that third hand may do once the case is on their desk: the arc gives them a copy of the argument and no way whatever to answer it, which means a plan may refer the same quarrel forever and never once be told what the hand it chose made of it.
